    "updated_at": "2024-10-18T14:51:06Z",
    "body": "> you propose to change, in https://www.w3.org/TR/epub-33/#sec-metadata-last-modified, the reference to xmlschema-2 to iso 8601\r\n\r\nRight, it's kind of odd that we use two different standards to refer to date/time formats when one will do. And unlike dc:date, the dcterms:modified definition is strictly controlled, so it's not like the date standard we use has any real influence over what is valid. Last modified dates are always iso 8601 conformant, so let's just consistently use that standard.",
